class.description:
[CgamePathTracer] bakes per-vertex lighting and ambient occlusion and renders still images on the CPU, using a [CgameBVH] for ray queries. It shades each surface hit with sun next-event estimation plus cosine-sampled diffuse bounces terminated by Russian roulette.
Work is distributed with [WorkerThreadPool]. Every vertex and every pixel owns its own PCG32 random stream derived from the seed and its index, so results are identical for a given seed regardless of the number of threads. Different seeds give independent estimates.
[b]Conventions:[/b] [code]sun_dir[/code] is the direction the sunlight travels (like the forward direction of a directional light). [code]sun_color[/code] is the radiance returned by a white diffuse surface facing the sun, with irradiance divided by pi already folded in. [code]sky_color[/code] is a constant-radiance environment. All colors are linear.
The baking and one-shot rendering functions are static. For progressive refinement, create an instance, call [method begin_progressive], then call [method accumulate] repeatedly and read the running estimate with [method to_image], [method to_linear_image], or [method get_pixel].
[codeblock]
var bvh := CgameBVH.new()
bvh.build(triangles)
var ao := CgamePathTracer.bake_ambient_occlusion(bvh, vertices, normals, 32, 4.0, 1)

var tracer := CgamePathTracer.new()
tracer.begin_progressive(Vector2i(256, 192), 7)
var light := CgamePathTracer.make_light(Vector3(-0.3, -1, -0.2), Color(1, 1, 1), Color(0.3, 0.4, 0.6))
for pass in 16:
    tracer.accumulate(bvh, camera_transform, 50.0, 1, light)
var image := tracer.to_image()
[/codeblock]
